            <ArticleTitle>A rare case of Eagle syndrome and diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis in the cervical spine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-170</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Published case studies involving diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis (DISH) along with symptomatic ossification of the stylohyoid ligament, or &quot;Eagle syndrome,&quot; are rare. In this report, we document a case of bilateral Eagle syndrome and advanced DISH in the cervical spine of an 80-year-old man who presented with severe neck stiffness and intermittent asphyxia. The key imaging and clinical features of this disorder are also described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
